            "creation_time": "2026-11-17T05:54:44Z",
            "creator": "kevinushey",
            "bug_id": 19330,
            "text": "## Summary\n\nThis patch restores `pow()` accuracy, within about half an ulp, for `x^3` and `x^4` with non-integer |x| <= 11, which since R 4.6.0 are computed as `x*x*x` and `x*x*x*x` (up to 1.3 and 2 ulp off). Small integer powers stay exact on every platform.\n\n## Details\n\nr89376 added a shortcut to `R_pow()` in `src/main/arithmetic.c` for `y == 3, 4` and |x| <= 11. It makes small integer powers exact without the system `pow()`; for other x the products round two or three times, so of 200k random non-integer x in (-11, 11), 25% of `x^3` and 35% of `x^4` are not correctly rounded, against 0.1% with `pow()` (macOS arm64). As `R_pow()` is API, C code calling it benefits too.\n\nReproducible example: attached as `pow-small-integer-repro.R`; it prints `within_1_ulp` TRUE for all eight arguments in R 4.5.3 and with the patch, FALSE in R 4.6.x.\n\nProposed patch: attached as `pow-small-integer.diff`, against trunk r90915. It keeps the shortcut for integer x (`x == (int) x`) and adds a reg-test; `make check` passes.\n\nFound while working on [PR#19286](https://bugs.r-project.org/show_bug.cgi?id=19286); the patch is independent of the one there.\n\nThe patch is also submitted as https://github.com/r-devel/r-svn/pull/501, where CI results can be seen.",
